","shillong"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"The Bishop Falls is located in Shillong, in the Indian state of Meghalaya. It is the 22nd highest waterfalls in India.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Bishop Falls (India)"},{"id":"shillong_shillong_peak","areaId":"shillong","name":"Shillong Peak","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":25.54738,"lng":91.87506},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"shillong_shillong_peak","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":3,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["shillongpeak","shillong"],"summary":"The highest point in the state of Meghalaya (1965 meters above sea level). There is a view-point where you can get breathtaking view of Shillong city. Peak is easily accessible from the Upper Shillong or Jowai Road. The city view during night is a scene to remember. It is host to a radar station for Indian Air Force and tourists are advised to declare their cameras while reaching view-point and no","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Shillong","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Shillong_from_Shillong_Peak.jpg/1280px-Shillong_from_Shillong_Peak.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Shillong_from_Shillong_Peak.jpg/500px-Shillong_from_Shillong_Peak.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Aadri","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shillong_from_Shillong_Peak.jpg"}},{"id":"shillong_wv_don_bosco_museum_of_indigenous_north_east_cultur","areaId":"shillong","name":"Don Bosco Museum of Indigenous North East Culture","category":"museum","tags":["museums"],"location":{"lat":25.59312,"lng":91.88235},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"shillong_wv_don_bosco_museum_of_indigenous_north_east_cultur","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":1,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"