"shillong","name":"Lady Hydari Park","category":"park","tags":["nature","photo"],"location":{"lat":25.56542,"lng":91.88162},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"shillong_wv_lady_hydari_park","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["ladyhydaripark","shillong"],"bestLight":"golden","summary":"The park has a variety of local flowering plants and orchids. It also has a small zoo within it. Children will like it as there are few swings, sea-saws, slips for them. It is a famous picnic spot for local population. This park is named after the Lady Hydari, the first lady of the state, wife of the Governor of Assam. This park has a mini zoo and a deer park, which is spread over more than one ki","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Shillong","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Ducks_in_lake_in_Shillong.jpg/1280px-Ducks_in_lake_in_Shillong.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Ducks_in_lake_in_Shillong.jpg/500px-Ducks_in_lake_in_Shillong.jpg","w":1200,"h":675,"author":"Sanat5357","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ducks_in_lake_in_Shillong.jpg"}},{"id":"shillong_lok_bhavan","areaId":"shillong","name":"Lok Bhavan","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":25.57278,"lng":91.88861},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"shillong_lok_bhavan","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["lokbhavan","shillong"],"summary":"The official residence of the Governor of Meghalaya appointed by the President of India, formerly the Raj Bhavan. It was built in 1903 as the Government House, resembling a typical English country cottage. It was designed to be earthquake-proof.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Shillong","photo":{"url